Next, we looked at the locations where the events occurred. The \(x\) and \(y\) positions of the events come from the track and vertex reconstruction. The event's \(z\) coordinate comes from the (drift length) = (drift time) \(\times\) (drift velocity). The drift velocity (\(v_{\rm drift}\)) is obtained by doing a TPC laser [137] calibration before each run. A laser run between runs 2329089 and 2329091 indicated that \(v_{\rm drift}=5.542\) cm/\(\mu\)s.

