### 6.5 Pseudorapidity Density

To obtain the corrected pseudorapidity density of charged particles (\(dN_{\rm ch}/d\eta\)), first the invariant yield (equation (6.23)) was numerically integrated from \(m_{T}-m_{0}\) = 0 to 10 GeV/c\({}^{2}\). This gives \(dN/dy\), which we then used \(\partial y/\partial\eta\sim\Delta y/\Delta\eta\) to estimate \(dN_{\rm ch}/d\eta\).

\[A \equiv \frac{d^{2}N}{2\pi m_{T}\,dm_{T}\,dy} \tag{6.23}\] \[\frac{dN}{dy}(m_{T}-m_{0}) = A\times 2\pi m_{T}\,dm_{T}\] (6.24) \[\frac{dN}{d\eta}(m_{T}-m_{0}) = \frac{dN}{dy}(m_{T}-m_{0})\times\frac{\Delta y}{\Delta\eta}(y,m_{ T}-m_{0},m_{0})\] (6.25) \[\frac{dN}{d\eta} = \int\frac{dN}{d\eta}(m_{T}-m_{0})\,dm_{T} \tag{6.26}\]

where \(\Delta y/\Delta\eta=(y_{\rm hi}-y_{\rm lo})/(\eta_{\rm hi}-\eta_{\rm ho})\). \(\eta\) can be calculated from \(m_{T}-m_{0}\), \(m_{0}\), and \(y\).

Table C.13 lists \(dN_{\rm ch}/d\eta\) values for each (rapidity, centrality) bin. The values are relatively higher than the reference multiplicity, \(N_{\rm ch}\) (defined in 3.3), which are used to determine centrality.

